# Virtual Environment (.venv) Structure Example
# 
# The Python virtual environment is initialized locally using:
#   python -m venv .venv
#
# Standard .venv directory layout:
# .venv/
# ├── Include/
# ├── Lib/
# │   └── site-packages/
# ├── Scripts/          # (Windows)
# │   ├── activate
# │   ├── Activate.ps1
# │   └── python.exe
# ├── bin/              # (macOS / Linux)
# │   ├── activate
# │   └── python
# └── pyvenv.cfg
#
# How to activate:
# - Windows (PowerShell): .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
# - Windows (cmd.exe):   .venv\Scripts\activate.bat
# - Linux / macOS:       source .venv/bin/activate
